{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310653,"nonce":"sD5Y1v+EoySv3p8c9Hm9bTxVEek=","title":"A named function declaration binds no name — one root cause behind ~15-20 conformance 'Cannot find name' failures. Attempted fix reverted; ...","message":"**A named function declaration binds no name.** `function foo() return 7; foo();`\ngives `Cannot find name 'foo'`, while `var foo = () -\u003e 7;` works — because there\nthe **`var`** does the binding, not the function.\n\n**Root cause.** `compiler/src/tast/ast_lowering/expr/mod.rs` (`ExprKind::Function`\narm) lowers to an anonymous `FunctionLiteral` and **never reads `func.name`**. The\nparser preserves it (`parser::Function { name: String, .. }`); lowering drops it.\n\nSame defect, two surfaces:\n- **local**: `function foo() ...` in a method body\n- **module-level**: `function helper() ...` at file scope, which additionally\n  goes through `lower_module_field` → `lower_function_object` → a global holding\n  a *closure value* that no call site dispatches through.\n\n\n- **Recursion is fine.** `fib` in the benchmark is a `public static function` on\n  a class (class-method path). Recursive class methods work.\n- **Ternaries are fine.** `n \u003c= 1 ? 1 : 99` and a recursive class method written\n  with one both give correct results.\n\n\nBind the name in the ENCLOSING scope *before* `enter_scope`, emit a\n`VarDeclarationExpr`, and add `ExprKind::Function` to the statement-conversion\nmatch in BOTH `decls/fields.rs` and `expr/mod.rs` (that match is keyed on the\n**parser** node — `ExprKind::Var`/`Final` — so a `VarDeclarationExpr` from a\nfunction fell through as a bare expression and produced `[E0100] variable\ndeclaration`).\n\nResult: simple named locals ✓, closure capture ✓, arrow/anon unaffected ✓.\n\n**Two blockers, both reproduced:**\n1. **Recursion** → `[E0100] Captured variable Symbol...`. The name is bound\n   before the body, so the body CAPTURES it — but the closure is built from that\n   same variable, so the self-reference captures an unassigned slot. Needs a\n   late-bound self-reference (allocate closure, then patch its own slot), i.e. a\n   change to closure environment layout, not to name binding.\n2. **`function foo(?v:Dynamic = true)`** → SIGABRT (was a clean error). Optional-\n   argument defaults die once resolution succeeds. **Regression in kind — this\n   alone disqualified shipping it.**\n\n**Module-level needs BOTH** routing (`lower_function_declaration` →\n`typed_file.functions`, which `tast_to_hir` already lowers properly) **and** scope\nregistration — `create_variable` uses `ScopeId::invalid()`, so the symbol resolves\nnowhere. Routing alone still reports `Cannot find name`. Fixing scope alone is\nWORSE: the name resolves to an uncallable global, the call lowers to `const 0`,\nand the program silently prints nothing instead of failing.\n\nRepro dirs: `scratchpad/lf_*` (local), `scratchpad/ml_*` (module-level).\nWorth ~15-20 corpus tests.\n\n\n`ExprKind::Function(func)` lowered to `TypedExpressionKind::FunctionLiteral`\nand DROPPED `func.name`. Fixed in `ast_lowering/expr/mod.rs`, the\n`ExprKind::Block` statement loop: a `Function` element with a non-empty name now\nbinds a variable symbol and emits `TypedStatement::VarDeclaration`, the same\nshape `Var`/`Final` already use. Plain and outer-capturing local functions work.\n\n**WHY RECURSION IS STILL BROKEN, and why binding earlier will NOT fix it:**\n`compute_captures` (tast_to_hir.rs ~5683) hard-codes\n`mode: HirCaptureMode::ByValue` for EVERY capture -- `ByRef`/`ByMutableRef`\nexist in the enum and are never selected. Bind the name before lowering the body\nand the body captures its own still-uninitialised slot BY VALUE. That is the\n\"recursive self-capture\" SIGABRT the earlier attempt hit; it is not an ordering\nbug. A real fix needs the self-referencing local lowered as a named function\nrather than a capturing closure, or a by-ref self-binding.\n\nRecursion currently ERRORS (`Cannot find name`), it does not miscompile -- keep\nit that way.\n\n**Also open, separate:** the RD parser rejects `inline` before a local function\n(`inline function foo(?v = true) ...` -\u003e \"expected expression, found 'inline'\",\nthen falls back to the legacy parser and fails differently). Issue5260 needs\nthis, not the binding fix.\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): `function foo()...; foo()` = Cannot find name; `func.name` is DROPPED at lowering. NOT recursion/ternary (both fine). Fix reverted: recursive self-capture + optarg SIGABRT.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_named_function_declarations_bind_no_name` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}